  "conclusions": [
    "A capture median decreases 60.1245 ->33.467ms and worker activation median 50.623 ->25.193ms; foreground request median decreases 26.8565 ->13.465ms. This is not a controlled causal estimate.",
    "Tails are not fixed: capture maximum 114.197 ->201.411ms, worker activation 95.191 ->123.334ms, foreground request 55.822 ->59.564ms, request delivery 40.572 ->46.750ms, reply delivery 8.696 ->58.697ms.",
    "All 13 new request traces are present. Submission checkpoint maximum is 0.012ms and write-completion duration maximum 0.020ms; receive maximum is 46.740ms. The slowest request has submit 0.010ms, completion 0.012ms and receive 46.740ms. The remaining request stall is after submission/rapid writer completion, including pipe transit, worker reader scheduling and decode, not app write-lock admission. No network traversal is involved in this local pipe span.",
    "The 201.411ms capture sample includes 120.656ms worker activation, 59.564ms foreground request nested inside activation and 46.740ms request receive. A separate 190.523ms capture has 123.334ms activation and 58.697ms reply delivery. Do not add nested foreground timing to activation.",
    "A nearby one-minute runtime summary records timer lateness 108.473ms, sampler lateness 674.367ms and nine runnable-delay samples in the >10ms..<=100ms bucket. This supports scheduling pressure as a remaining risk, but does not prove the exact OS/API stall cause.",
    "One reconnect episode is retained. A explicitly records trigger fault_trust_freshness_expired while trust_active_prelock_lockfile_acl_query is in progress; B records trigger fault_remote_eof and four network-reset acquisition attempts. The shared connection changed and then recovered automatically. Exact cross-PC event order cannot be inferred from wall clocks; the matched profiles show about a five-second wall-clock offset.",
    "A trust-expiry disconnect is the direct recorded trigger; whether the ACL syscall itself or execution scheduling consumed the freshness budget is not yet isolated.",
    "No new protected-service FAULTED/poison/recovery-required label is retained, and both service/input states are READY. Recovery lastFailure entries are historical and predate g527. A later heartbeat response failure is followed by refresh_joined and protected_ready about 0.849s later without another peer reconnect.",
    "B tails also increased: preparation maximum 32.414 ->127.340ms and worst input maximum 15.657 ->151.942ms. Do not describe this trial as globally smooth or recurrence-free."
  ],
